<article>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-11-17">17 November 2026</time>.</p>

    <p>This policy covers <a href="/">pennydreadfulmagic.com</a> and the mtgbot Discord application, also called MTG Bot, operated by the Penny Dreadful community. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:hello@pennydreadfulmagic.com">hello@pennydreadfulmagic.com</a>.</p>

    <h2 id="information">Information we process</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Discord messages and commands.</strong> Where Discord and server permissions allow it, mtgbot receives messages, command arguments and interactions, including the associated user, server, channel and message identifiers. It uses this information to respond to commands, recognize <code>[[card name]]</code> references, display card information and provide community features. It can also process reactions and messages in a server's configured moderation channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Discord profiles and presence.</strong> The bot can access usernames, display names, roles and server membership information made available by Discord. Where presence access is enabled, it can process online status and activities to support streaming roles and achievement-role updates.</li>
        <li><strong>Linked accounts and community records.</strong> Signing in through Discord gives the website access to your Discord identifier, profile information and server information needed for sign-in and permissions. We keep session authorization information and, if you link accounts, the association between your Discord identifier and Magic Online username. We also store submitted decks, league registrations, match results and related community records.</li>
        <li><strong>Website requests and preferences.</strong> Requests can include your IP address, browser information, requested URL and referrer. Cookies support sign-in, sessions and display preferences; browser storage also remembers preferences such as dark mode. Blocking these may prevent sign-in or preference features from working.</li>
        <li><strong>Diagnostics and support.</strong> Application and server logs, error reports and support messages can contain command arguments, identifiers, request information and message content involved in an error. mtgbot's application log files rotate by size; other server logs and diagnostic systems have their own retention settings. We do not promise that all message content is processed only in memory.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="use">How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to operate the website and bot, answer requests, link accounts, run leagues and tournaments, maintain community roles, moderate configured channels, diagnose failures and respond to support or privacy requests. Some features depend on the permissions granted to the bot and may not be available in every server.</p>
    <p>We do not sell Discord user data, use it for targeted advertising, or use Discord message content to train machine-learning or AI models.</p>

    <h2 id="sharing">Public information and service providers</h2>
    <p>Bot replies are visible to the people who can access the channel unless a feature explicitly provides a private response. Decklists, Magic Online usernames, league and tournament results, achievements and linked-account lookups can be public. Do not put sensitive information into public commands or bug reports.</p>
    <p>Commands that report bugs can publish the report text and reporting username as an issue on GitHub. Website errors and performance reports can also create GitHub issues containing diagnostic and request information. Error monitoring uses Sentry when configured and can receive error context. These reports may include personal information; contact us if a report needs attention or removal.</p>
    <p>We use hosting and diagnostic services to run these tools. Requests for card data, prices, player information and other command results can contact services such as Scryfall, Gatherling and Google Custom Search. The information sent depends on the feature: for example, a card or search query, or a Discord identifier for an account lookup. We also exchange information with Discord to authenticate users, receive events and send responses. Those services operate under their own privacy policies. We may disclose information when required by law.</p>

    <h2 id="retention">Storage and retention</h2>
    <p>Information can be held in application memory, caches, databases, session storage, logs and diagnostic services. Linked-account associations remain until they are unlinked or deleted. League queues and some caches expire automatically; public competition records are retained as community history. There is no single fixed retention period for all logs and records.</p>
    <p>We retain personal information only for as long as needed for the purposes described here, including resolving errors and maintaining community records, or as required by law. Deletion requests are handled for the relevant systems, including service providers where applicable. Copies in backups, where present, may remain until those backups are replaced. Public copies made by other people or independent services may remain outside our control.</p>

    <h2 id="choices">Your choices and deletion requests</h2>
    <p>You can stop using the bot, revoke the website's authorization in Discord's Authorized Apps settings, and ask us by email to unlink your Discord and Magic Online accounts. Server administrators can restrict the bot's channel permissions or remove it. These controls do not automatically erase information already stored, published results or diagnostic reports.</p>
    <p>To request access, correction or deletion of your personal information, or to object to its processing, email <a href="mailto:hello@pennydreadfulmagic.com">hello@pennydreadfulmagic.com</a>. Tell us your Discord user ID or Magic Online username and what information your request concerns. We may ask you to verify that the account is yours; we will never ask for your password or bot token. We will explain any information that must be retained and any limits on the request. Please send privacy requests by email rather than posting personal information in a public GitHub issue.</p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We will publish updates on this page and revise the date above when this policy changes. You can contact us at <a href="/contact/">Contact Us</a> with questions about this policy or the services it covers.</p>
</article>
